''Wait, you're telling me that this flimsy piece of cloth will somehow protect me? I was expecting something like, you know, actual armor or at least something more sturdy than a scarf.''

A peculiar scarf of unknown make, it somehow increases the user's defense and resistance even though it appears to be nothing more than a piece of cloth that provides nothing in the way of actual protection.
^green;+10% GENERAL Resistance.^reset;

''Don't you think that perhaps maybe the Guild Master likes Perfect Apples just a little bit *too* much?''
A badge of unknown make that is typically issued to Guild Masters of an Exploration Team Guild or to highly esteemed and experienced veteran Explorers who has truly distinguished themselves.
^green;Grants Tier 6 Vanilla Armour bonuses and provides oxygen and protection against all ^yellow;[VANILLA] ^green;Environmental Hazards.^reset;
^cyan;If Frackin' Universe is installed, it provides ^orange;[Moderate Immunity] ^cyan;against Heat, Cold, and Radiation Environmental Hazards.^reset;

''I look a little bit silly you say? Why, with these babies, I sure won't miss the next Gravlerock I throw! Now lets go talk to the brothers and stock up before we take the next job at that dungeon.''
A peculiar pair of spectacles unknown make. It somehow makes the user more accurate even though it doesn't appear to possess any sort of smart targeting and tracking functionality such as those found on Ballistic CPUs or on an FCS unit.
^green;Increases Weapon Proficiency by 20%^reset;

''So, exactly how does this pink scarf protects me against poison?''
A pink colored scarf of unknown make, it somehow protects the user from the effect of poison and other similar effects.
^green;Grants immunity towards standard Vanilla Poison status effects, standard Vanilla Radiation, [GIC] Immense Radiation, and prevents certain [GIC] environmental hazards.^reset;
^cyan;If Frackin' Universe is installed, it provides ^orange;[Moderate Immunity] ^cyan;against Radiation Environmental Hazards.^reset;

''I know we just met, and you have amnesia and all that. But I think we make a great team back there, so I was wondering if well... you know, want to form an Exploration Team with me?''

A sky blue colored bow of unknown make, it is said that it resonates deeply with those who possess a certain type of Aura.

^green;Slightly increases Defense, Attack, GENERAL Resistance, and Weapon Proficiency by 5%.^reset;

Seen as a cheaper counterpart and alternative to the more expensive EOTech sight, the HD-33 Holographic Sight is optimized for close to mid range target acquirement with an open circle and dot reticle for easy tracking of targets.


^orange;+20% [EWS] Hit Chance and Accuracy when moving.^reset;

^green;Right-click on a compatible GiC Weapon to attach.^reset;

The PU Scope is a simple 3.5× power (that can be increased to 6.5× power through the use of an aftermarket objective lens which this one sadly does not have) magnified sniper scope that was originally introduced on Earth in 1940 with the SVT-40 rifle.

^orange;+10% [EWS] Hit Chance and Accuracy when stationary.^reset;

^green;Right-click on a compatible GiC Weapon to attach.^reset;

''This is Station to Observer coordinates received, friendly Goshawk is inbound for a rocket run.''

^orange;Hydra 70 Rocket Strafe:^reset; Fires a ^yellow;non-damaging beacon^reset; that ^orange;calls upon a Goshawk Fightercraft with Hydra 70 Rocket Pods to strafe the target zone.^reset; Strafing begins from left-to-right.
^yellow;Requires decent space, but can work underground | Reloads using Cracked Red Suns.^reset;
^orange;Tap Right-Click to Fire/Reload the Coordinator.^reset;

''I don't care or give a shit if it's a magical pony flying through the sky, JUST SHOOT IT DOWN!'' 
ZSU-23-4 Shilka Turret Close in Weapons System (starship point defense replica production model): Fires a ^yellow;non-damaging beacon^reset; that ^orange;directs your ship to fire a short barrage of high explosive 23mm shells at the impact site of the beacon.^reset;
^yellow;Requires decent space, but can work underground via use of teleporter munitions | Reloads using Healing Flasks.^reset;
^orange;Tap Right-Click to Fire/Reload the Coordinator.^reset;

The Advanced Tactical Smart Gunsight is a high-magnification sight with a built-in ballistic CPU and rangefinder that can accurately measure out to 10km. Intended to help track and engage targets at extreme ranges with CCIP (Constantly Computed Impact Point), the ATACS-GS is useful for those wishing to push the maximum effective range of their weapons to their absolute limits.
^orange;+25% Weapon Proficiency after 0.5s of not running, firing, or being shot.^reset;
^green;Right-click on a compatible GiC Weapon to attach.^reset;

''Now. Take your talons, rip open your stomach, and show everyone what you're really like inside. Pour out your life on this stage.''
An advanced thermal smart scope that allows the user to stalk and engage targets in complete darkness.
^#96CBE7;Highlights targets in a 50-degree angle from the gun | 100 Block Range | Cannot see through walls.^reset;
^orange;+15% Standing Weapon Proficiency.^reset;
^green;Right-click on a compatible GiC Weapon to attach.^reset;

