''Why does my shotgun need to connect to Bluetooth and Wi-Fi?''
Russia's first ''Smart Shotgun'' the MP-155 Ultima is essentially a very fancy furniture kit for the MP-155 semi-automatic shotgun that adds various sorts of enhanced capabilities that includes a built-in computer and camera system with wireless connectivity with various sorts of other devices. Accepts 12 Gauge shells.
^cyan;Comes with a thermal camera sight that can optionally be removed and replaced with other sight attachments.^reset;
^orange;Can jam, unlike other shotguns.^reset;

The Sjögren Inertia Shotgun is a semi-automatic shotgun of Swedish origin that implemented the then-new and innovative inertia-operated system. While only a small number of this shotgun was initially produced in the early 20th century, the novelty and unique design of the shotgun have seen a resurgence in recent times in new reproduction models. 

Accepts 12 Gauge shells.
^orange;Can jam, unlike other shotguns.^reset;

